      "explain": "An <strong>elementary row operation</strong> is one of three allowed changes to the rows of a matrix. They are allowed because they <strong>never change the rank</strong> of the matrix, and when the matrix represents a system of equations they <strong>never change its solutions</strong> — they only make it look simpler.",
