      "worked": "<strong>Write this system in matrix form.</strong><br>x + y + z = 6<br>x + 2y + 3z = 14<br>x + 4y + 7z = 30<br><br><strong>Coefficient matrix A:</strong><br>[ 1 &nbsp; 1 &nbsp; 1 ]<br>[ 1 &nbsp; 2 &nbsp; 3 ]<br>[ 1 &nbsp; 4 &nbsp; 7 ]<br><br><strong>Unknowns X = ( x, y, z )ᵀ &nbsp;·&nbsp; Constants B = ( 6, 14, 30 )ᵀ</strong><br><br><strong>Augmented matrix [A | B]:</strong><br>[ 1 &nbsp; 1 &nbsp; 1 &nbsp; | &nbsp; 6 &nbsp;]<br>[ 1 &nbsp; 2 &nbsp; 3 &nbsp; | &nbsp;14 ]<br>[ 1 &nbsp; 4 &nbsp; 7 &nbsp; | &nbsp;30 ]<br><br>Number of unknowns <strong>n = 3</strong>. This one grid now contains the complete system — and in the next topic it decides the whole question of consistency.",
