      "explain": "A system AX = B is <strong>consistent</strong> if it has at least one solution. The test compares <strong>rank(A)</strong>, <strong>rank([A | B])</strong> and <strong>n</strong>, the number of unknowns. If the two ranks differ, there is no solution at all. If they are equal, the system is consistent — and whether the solution is unique depends on how the common rank compares with n.",
