3z = 14 &nbsp;·&nbsp; x + 3y + 2z = 13 &nbsp;&nbsp;(n = 3)<br>[ 1 &nbsp; 1 &nbsp; 1 &nbsp;| &nbsp;6 ]<br>[ 1 &nbsp; 2 &nbsp; 3 &nbsp;| &nbsp;14 ]<br>[ 1 &nbsp; 3 &nbsp; 2 &nbsp;| &nbsp;13 ]<br><strong>R2 → R2 − R1:</strong> ( 0, 1, 2 | 8 ) &nbsp;·&nbsp; <strong>R3 → R3 − R1:</strong> ( 0, 2, 1 | 7 )<br><strong>R3 → R3 − 2R2:</strong> ( 0, 0, 1−4 | 7−16 ) = ( 0, 0, −3 | −9 )<br>[ 1 &nbsp; 1 &nbsp; &nbsp;1 &nbsp;| &nbsp;6 ]<br>[ 0 &nbsp; 1 &nbsp; &nbsp;2 &nbsp;| &nbsp;8 ]<br>[ 0 &nbsp; 0 &nbsp; −3 &nbsp;| &nbsp;−9 ]<br><strong>rank(A) = rank([A|B]) = 3 = n → unique solution.</strong><br><em>Back substitution:</em> −3z = −9 → <strong>z = 3</strong>; then y + 2(3) = 8 → <strong>y = 2</strong>; then x + 2 + 3 = 6 → <strong>x = 1</strong>.<br><em>Check:</em> 1+2+3 = 6 ✅ &nbsp; 1+4+9 = 14 ✅ &nbsp; 1+6+6 = 13 ✅",
