      "examAnswer": "A system of linear equations AX = B is said to be consistent if it possesses at least one solution. By the Rouché–Capelli theorem, the system is consistent if and only if the rank of the coefficient matrix A is equal to the rank of the augmented matrix [A | B]. If these ranks are unequal the system is inconsistent and has no solution. If the ranks are equal and their common value r equals n, the number of unknowns, the system possesses a unique solution; if r is less than n, the system possesses infinitely many solutions involving n − r arbitrary parameters. A homogeneous system AX = O is always consistent, since the trivial solution X = O always satisfies it, and it possesses a non-trivial solution if and only if the rank of A is less than n.",
