      "worked": "<strong>Find the eigenvectors of A = [ 4 &nbsp;1 ; 2 &nbsp;3 ], whose eigenvalues are λ = 2 and λ = 5.</strong><br><br><strong>Case λ = 5:</strong><br>A − 5I = [ 4−5 &nbsp; 1 ; 2 &nbsp; 3−5 ] = [ −1 &nbsp; 1 ; 2 &nbsp; −2 ]<br>The equations are: &nbsp; −x₁ + x₂ = 0 &nbsp; and &nbsp; 2x₁ − 2x₂ = 0<br>Both say the same thing: <strong>x₂ = x₁</strong> (the second row is just −2 times the first).<br>Take x₁ = 1 → <strong>X₁ = ( 1, 1 )ᵀ</strong><br><em>Verify AX₁ = 5X₁:</em><br>AX₁ = ( 4(1) + 1(1), &nbsp; 2(1) + 3(1) ) = ( 5, 5 ) = 5 × ( 1, 1 ) ✅<br><br><strong>Case λ = 2:</strong><br>A − 2I = [ 4−2 &nbsp; 1 ; 2 &nbsp; 3−2 ] = [ 2 &nbsp; 1 ; 2 &nbsp; 1 ]<br>The equations are: &nbsp; 2x₁ + x₂ = 0 &nbsp; and &nbsp; 2x₁ + x₂ = 0 — identical.<br>So <strong>x₂ = −2x₁</strong>. Take x₁ = 1 → <strong>X₂ = ( 1, −2 )ᵀ</strong><br><em>Verify AX₂ = 2X₂:</em><br>AX₂ = ( 4(1) + 1(−2), &nbsp; 2(1) + 3(−2) ) = ( 2, −4 ) = 2 × ( 1, −2 ) ✅<br><br><strong>Answer:</strong> λ = 5 with eigenvector ( 1, 1 )ᵀ, and λ = 2 with eigenvector ( 1, −2 )ᵀ.<br><em>Note:</em> ( 3, 3 )ᵀ and ( −1, −1 )ᵀ are equally correct answers for λ = 5 — any non-zero multiple works.",
